en, becauſe each of them poſſeſſeth the whole man, though not wholly. There are by their means two I’s in every believer, Rom. vii. 15. For that which I do, I allow not: for what I would, that do I not; but what I hate, that do I. There is not one part of the man that is in Chriſt, but grace has a part of it, and corruption has a part of it: as in the twilight there is light over all, and darkneſs over all too, the darkneſs being mixed in every part with the light. So my renewed part is I, a man having an underſtanding enlightened, a will renewed, affections ſpiritualized, uſing my body conform: but my unrenewed part is I too, having an underſtanding darkened, a will rebellious, affections corrupted, and uſing my body accordingly.","frame_run_id":2,"frame_seq":1,"frame_ts_ms":1792281246071,"id":"i|noun|2","lemma":"i","norm":"i","pos":"noun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:countable","tag:uncountable","qual:metaphysics","pos_raw:noun"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":["me#Noun"],"token_index":0,"word":"i"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(letter, uppercase) The ninth letter of the English alphabet, called i and written in the Latin script.","example":null,"frame_run_id":2,"frame_seq":1,"frame_ts_ms":1792281246071,"id":"i|phrase|5","lemma":"i","norm":"i","pos":"phrase","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","tag:letter","tag:uppercase","pos_raw:character"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"i"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(alt-of, ordinal, uppercase, number) The ordinal number ninth, derived from this letter of the English alphabet, called i and written in the Latin script.","example":null,"frame_run_id":2,"frame_seq":1,"frame_ts_ms":1792281246071,"id":"i|numeral|2","lemma":"i","norm":"i","pos":"numeral","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","tag:alt-of","tag:ordinal","tag:uppercase","rtag:number","pos_raw:num"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"i"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(roadway, us, countable, uncountable) Interstate.","