y galaxies there are in the universe.","frame_run_id":8,"frame_seq":7,"frame_ts_ms":1792284481011,"id":"the|determiner|2","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Used to indicate a certain example of (a noun) which is usually of most concern or most common or familiar.","example":"No one in the whole country had seen it before.","frame_run_id":8,"frame_seq":7,"frame_ts_ms":1792284481011,"id":"the|determiner|3","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Used before a body part, a family member, a pet (especially of someone previously mentioned), as an alternative to a possessive pronoun.","example":"A stone hit him on the head. (= “A stone hit him on his head.”)","frame_run_id":8,"frame_seq":7,"frame_ts_ms":1792284481011,"id":"the|determiner|4","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(colloquial) Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Precedes a familiar nickname or other term of address.","example":"How's the Sal today?","frame_run_id":8,"frame_seq":7,"frame_ts_ms":1792284481011,"id":"the|determiner|5","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:colloquial","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Used in many idiomatic expressions and proverbs to refer to common objects, roles, or situations connected with something definite, in the manner of an analogy","example":"square the circle; feel the pinch; beat around the bush; throw the baby out with the bathwater","frame_run_id":8,"frame_seq":7,"frame_ts_ms":1792284481011,"id":"the|determiner|6","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — When stressed, indicates that it describes something which is considered to be best or exclusively worthy of attention.","example":"That is the hospital to go to for heart surgery.","frame_run_id":8,"frame_seq":7,"frame_ts_ms":1792284481011,"id":"the|determiner|7","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — Used before a noun phrase beginning with superlative or comparative adjective or an ordinal number, indicating that the noun refers to a single item.","example":"That was the juiciest apple pie e