ities or characteristics. — Indicates a quality or characteristic; \"characterized by\".","example":"Pooh was said to be a bear of very little brain.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284480549,"id":"of|preposition|33","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing qualities or characteristics. — Indicates quantity, age, price, etc.","example":"A young man of 20 has been paying interest at an exorbitant rate of 10%.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284480549,"id":"of|preposition|34","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(considered incorrect by some, us, informal) Expressing qualities or characteristics. — Used to link singular indefinite nouns (preceded by the indefinite article) and attributive adjectives modified by certain common adverbs of degree.","example":"It's not that big of a deal.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284480549,"id":"of|preposition|35","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","usage:region:american english","tag:us","tag:informal","qual:considered incorrect by some","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(regional) Expressing a point in time. — During the course of (a set period of time, day of the week etc.), now specifically with implied repetition or regularity.","example":"Of an evening, we would often go for a stroll along the river.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284480549,"id":"of|preposition|36","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:regional","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"anto