ing a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Precedes a familiar nickname or other term of address.","example":"How's the Sal today?","frame_run_id":2,"frame_seq":1,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487124,"gram_function":[],"id":"the|determiner|5","lemma":"the","mw":false,"norm":"the","pos":"determiner","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:colloquial","pos_raw:article"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Used in many idiomatic expressions and proverbs to refer to common objects, roles, or situations connected with something definite, in the manner of an analogy","example":"square the circle; feel the pinch; beat around the bush; throw the baby out with the bathwater","frame_run_id":2,"frame_seq":1,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487124,"gram_function":[],"id":"the|determiner|6","lemma":"the","mw":false,"norm":"the","pos":"determiner","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — When stressed, indicates that it describes something which is considered to be best or exclusively worthy of attention.","example":"That is the hospital to go to for heart surgery.","frame_run_id":2,"frame_seq":1,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487124,"gram_function":[],"id":"the|determiner|7","lemma":"the","mw":false,"norm":"the","pos":"determiner","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"active_cells",