en location, place or time. Compare \"origin\" senses, above.","example":"He was perhaps the most famous scientist of the twentieth century.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|27","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing possession. — Belonging to (a place) through having title, ownership or control over it.","example":"The owner of the nightclub was arrested.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|28","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing possession. — Belonging to (someone or something) as something they possess or have as a characteristic; the \"possessive genitive\". (With abstract nouns, this intersects with the subjective genitive, above under \"agency\" senses.)","example":"Keep the handle of the saucepan away from the flames.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|29","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Forming the \"objective genitive\".","example":null,"frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"gram_function":[],"id":"of|preposition|30","lemma":"of","mw":false,"norm":"of","pos":"preposition","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Forming the \"objective genitive\". — Follows an agent noun, verbal noun or noun