e"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":6,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — Used before a noun phrase beginning with superlative or comparative adjective or an ordinal number, indicating that the noun refers to a single item.","example":"That was the juiciest apple pie ever.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"the|determiner|8","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":6,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — Introducing a singular term to be taken generically: preceding a name of something standing for a whole class.","example":"Stern and God-fearing, the Afrikaner takes his religion seriously.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"the|determiner|9","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":6,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — Used with the plural of a surname to indicate the entire family.","example":"The Bushes have held political office for several decades and the Kennedys longer.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"the|determiner|10","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":6,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used with an adjective — Added to a superlative or an ordinal number to make it into a substantive.","example":"That apple pie was the best.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"the|determiner|11","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":6