"bank|proper_noun|1","lemma":"bank","norm":"bank","pos":"proper_noun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","cat:en:places in england","cat:en:places in hampshire, england","cat:en:villages in england","cat:en:villages in hampshire, england","pos_raw:name"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"bank"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"A major London Underground station in the City of London, named after the Bank of England and one of the busiest stations on the network (OS grid ref TQ3281)","example":"Anybody familiar with the London Underground network will know that Bank Tube station is a place to be avoided - if at all possible - on a weekday morning. Located at the very heart of London's 'Square Mile' financial district, some 70,000 people detrain there during the morning peak, to pass through its gatelines and those at the adjoining station at Monument. A further 50,000 passengers squeeze into the station complex at exactly the same time of day, in order to change between the five lines that pass through it.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"bank|proper_noun|2","lemma":"bank","norm":"bank","pos":"proper_noun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:name"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"bank"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"A surname.","example":null,"frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"bank|proper_noun|3","lemma":"bank","norm":"bank","pos":"proper_noun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","cat:en:english surnames","pos_raw:name"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":4,"word":"bank"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(following a noun) Having partitive effect. — Indicates a given part.","example":"We want a larger slice of the cake.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"of|preposition|24","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:following a noun","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(except in phrases, dialectal, obsolete) Expressing distance or motion. — From (a place); off.","example":"Take the chicken out of the freezer.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"of|preposition|1","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:dialectal","tag:obsolete","qual:except in phrases","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(obsolete except in phrases) Expressing distance or motion. — Since, from (a given time, earlier state etc.).","example":"He hasn't been well of late.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"of|preposition|2","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","qual:obsolete except in phrases","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing distance or motion. — From, away from (a position, number, distance etc.).","example":"There are no shops within twenty miles of the cottage.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"of|preposition|3","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing separation. — Indicating removal, absence or separation, with the action indicated by a transitive verb and the quality or substance by a grammatical object.","example":"Finally she was relieved of the burden of caring for her sick husband.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"of|preposition|4","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing separation. — Indicating removal, absence or separation, with resulting state indicated by an adjective.","example":"He seemed devoid of human feelings.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"of|preposition|5","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(obsolete) Expressing separation. — Indicating removal, absence or separation, construed with an intransitive verb.","example":"He was kindly treated by the people at Saco, and recovered of his wounds.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"of|preposition|6","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:obsolete","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing origin. — Indicating an ancestral source or origin of descent.","example":"The word is believed to be of Japanese origin.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"of|preposition|7","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing origin. — Introducing an epithet that indicates a birthplace, residence, dominion, or other place associated with the individual.","example":"Jesus of Nazareth (after hometown)","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"of|preposition|8","lemma":"of","norm":"of","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":5,"word":"of"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Expressing origin. — Indicating a (non-physical) source of action or emotion; introducing a cause, instigation; from, out of, as an expression of.","example":"The invention was born of necessity.","frame_run_id":5,"frame_seq":4,"frame_ts_ms":1792284487790,"id":"of|preposition|9","lemma":